tionately  out of balance with the investment in  the qms  it almost seems absurd that investors  are willing to compromise the very  most foundational component of starting  up and operating a cannabis lab  neglecting to account for a qms is  costly but it doesn't need to be this  way  a hundred and fifty thousand dollar  investment in a qms and professional  support can completely flip the curve  from a cost of delay  to a positive return on on investment  delivering up to 2.7 million dollars of  value in the first 18 months  so where does all of this lead  clearly cannabis labs have a lot of  economic potential  and can be profitable investments the  number one reason they struggle to start  up and remain profitable  is because of an incorrect mindset that  loses sight of the ultimate value of its  services  most people consider a qms to be a  necessary evil of running a lab  and either try to avoid it or treat it  as another thing to do  however the mindset mindset needs to  shift to one that emphasizes the qms  as the way to work and by doing so  the lab will produce profitable results  beginning with the end in sight  meaning focusing on the predictability  accuracy  reliability and timeliness of test  results will ensure the laboratory  personnel and investors are always  working in the same direction  as such the qms sops and validation  protocols  should be considered just as important  as if not more important  than investments in instruments and  other physical assets required to  operate the lab  the laboratory personnel who ultimately  perform the billable work  should be considered the most important  resources of the lab  the lab must get the best people who are  competent and naturally committed to  quality  laboratory personnel should be provided  with training  and time to develop deeper competencies  in  all aspects of the work they perform as  well as with the qms  so is it too late if you've already  started  or have been operating a cannabis lab  without quality as a strategic  plan and an operational model  absolutely not it's never too late  to renew your commitment to quality and  convert to a robust management system  quality is the inevitable strategic plan  and operational model  labs that embrace this will have a  profitable business  for years to come thank you for your  time and attention today
 

